{
  "title": "Radiocarpal Fracture Dislocation",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/422863/radiocarpal-fracture-dislocation",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 13 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A radiocarpal dislocation (RCD) is the total loss of contact between the carpus and the radius.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is confirmed by orthogonal radiographs of the wrist.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually internal fixation of the fractured bones, radiocarpal pinning and repair of the radiocarpal ligaments.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "0.2% of injuries to the wrist annually",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male > females",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**dorsal dislocation > volar dislocation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "high-energy trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "high energy shear or **rotational force to a hyperextended and pronated wrist**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "often due to falls from height and motor vehicle accidents",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "orthopaedic conditions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "open fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "distal radius fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "radial styloid avulsion fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "attachment of the radioscaphocapitate (RSC) ligament",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "volar lunate facet fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "attachment of the short radiolunate ligament",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "ulnar styloid fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "carpal bone fractures (scaphoid, lunate and trapezium)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**medial nerve injury > ulnar nerve injury**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**irreducible DRUJ with soft tissue interposition**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "intercarpal injury (scapholunate or lunotriquetral dissociation)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osseous",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "distal radius",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "articular surface is biconcave and triangular with the radial styloid forming apex of triangle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sigmoid notch forms the base and articulates with head of the ulna",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "dorsal surface of distal radius is convex and serves as floor of the dorsal extensor compartments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ligamentous",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/422863/images/ligaments_of_the_wrist..jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "radiocarpal ligaments, capsule, and the scaphoid and lunate fossa of the distal radius provide stability to the radiocarpal joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**short radiolunate ligament** is the primary soft-tissue restraint against **volar translation** of the carpus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "short radiolunate ligament attaches to the **volar lunate facet** of the disal radius",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**radioscaphocapitate ligament (RSC)** provides restraint against **ulnar translation** of the carpus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "RSC ligament attaches to the **radial styloid**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "ulnolunate and ulnotriquitral ligaments originate on the volar side of the TFCC (which inserts into base of ulnar styloid)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
